'''Magic''' is a supernatural force that can be harnessed through the use of seals. Drawn with [[Conjuring Ink|conjuring ink]], seals generate magical effects known as spells. If someone possesses conjuring ink and a means to draw, they can cast magic. Those trained in the art of magic are called [[Witches|witches]].

==Seals==
[[File:Sylph Shoes Seal.png|thumb|136x136px]]
To cast a spell, one must first draw a seal. The size and precision of a seal have a strong effect on the quality of a spell: larger seals are more powerful than smaller ones, and neatly drawn seals are more stable and long-lasting than messy ones.{{Ref|m|1}}{{Ref|m|27}}{{Ref|m|13}} Seals are made from three primary parts: sigils, signs, and rings.

===Sigils===
''See main page, [[Sigils Explained]], for information on the effect of each sigil''

Sigils, typically placed in the center of a seal, control what type of spell a seal will generate, some special [[Decorative Sigils|Sigils]] directly correspond to a specific plant, animal or a manmade object. For instance, the [[Pyreball Seal|pyreball seal]], which creates a floating ball of flame, contains a fire sigil, the [[Watershot Seal|watershot seal]], which shoots a jet of water, contains a water sigil, and the [[Glowing Owlcat|Glowing Owlcat seal]], a spell that manifest an illusion of a small Owlcat, contains a version of the Owlcat sigil. While sigils are not required to create a functional spell, the vast majority contain at least one. The size of a sigil in relation to the ring determines the intensity and strength of the spell’s effect, with larger sigils creating more powerful effects compared to smaller ones.{{Ref|m|46}} Regardless of a sigil's location within a seal, it's behavior will be the same.

The four, main elemental sigils are known as the Primary Tetrad. They include fire, water, earth, and wind.
